Z||000000||yobtah||05-08-2000||09:07 PM||||I have an '87 SE V6 with 72,000 miles.  It's sometimes parked in a garage and sometimes parked outside.  When it has been in the garage, it starts and idles normally.  The problem occurs when it has been parked outside... then it starts perfectly, but it can't maintain a constant idle speed.  The engine speed varies from around 500 rpm to around 900 rpm.  If I try to drive the car before the engine warms at all, it stumbles and doesn't pull well at all.  After the engine has warmed slightly, it is able to hold a constant idle and it runs and pulls perfectly normally. I'm guessing the problem is related to humdity outdoors... that may explain the normal starting indoors.  I don't think it's related to outside temperature... it's the same temperature in the garage.  Any help with this is appreciated.  Thanks!||||reg||1
